# CompTIA A+ — Ports & Protocols

What port does FTP use for control traffic?
---
21
= port 21
---
Port 20 carries the data connection in active mode. The pair is listed as 20/21 on the exam.

What port does SSH use?
---
22
= port 22

What port does Telnet use?
---
23
= port 23
---
Unencrypted remote shell. SSH on 22 replaced it.

What port does SMTP use?
---
25
= port 25
---
Sending mail between servers. Clients usually submit on 587 with TLS.

What port does DNS use?
---
53
= port 53
---
UDP for ordinary lookups, TCP for zone transfers.

What ports does DHCP use?
---
67 and 68
= 67/68
= 67, 68
= 68 and 67
---
The server listens on UDP 67, the client on UDP 68.

What port does HTTP use?
---
80
= port 80

What port does POP3 use?
---
110
= port 110
---
Downloads mail to one device. IMAP on 143 keeps it on the server.

What port does IMAP use?
---
143
= port 143

What ports does SNMP use?
---
161 and 162
= 161/162
= 161, 162
= 162 and 161
---
Agents listen on UDP 161. Traps arrive at the manager on UDP 162.

What port does LDAP use?
---
389
= port 389
---
Directory lookups, such as Active Directory queries. LDAPS uses 636.

What port does HTTPS use?
---
443
= port 443

What port does SMB/CIFS use?
---
445
= port 445
---
Windows file and printer sharing. Older NetBIOS transport used 137-139.

What port does RDP use?
---
3389
= port 3389

Which protocol uses port 22?
---
SSH
= secure shell
---
SCP and SFTP ride on it too.

Which protocol uses port 3389?
---
RDP
= remote desktop protocol
= remote desktop

Which protocol uses port 445?
---
SMB
= CIFS
= SMB/CIFS
= server message block

Name three protocols that use UDP rather than TCP
---
quota: 3
attempts: 5
+ DHCP
+ DNS
+ SNMP
+ TFTP
+ NTP
---
DNS uses both, but ordinary lookups are UDP. TCP protocols to rule out: HTTP, HTTPS, SSH, FTP, Telnet, SMTP, RDP.
